57
00:01:56,048 --> 00:01:57,360
troubles stopped
them.

58
00:01:58,196 --> 00:02:00,089
Historians estimate
that more than twenty

59
00:02:00,158 --> 00:02:01,795
thousand workers
died.

60
00:02:02,366 --> 00:02:04,468
The United States
took over in nineteen

61
00:02:04,526 --> 00:02:05,328
oh four.

62
00:02:05,723 --> 00:02:07,673
Ten years later, on
the fifteenth of

63
00:02:07,743 --> 00:02:10,843
August, nineteen
fourteen, the first ship

64
00:02:11,179 --> 00:02:12,352
officially crossed.

65
00:02:12,747 --> 00:02:14,883
The American effort
cost almost five

66
00:02:14,929 --> 00:02:17,286
hundred million
dollars, and more than

67
00:02:17,379 --> 00:02:19,841
five thousand workers
lost their lives.

68
00:02:20,562 --> 00:02:22,895
At the end of
nineteen ninety-nine, the

69
00:02:22,953 --> 00:02:24,823
canal was handed
